If we decide to refactor the connective system, could {gi mu'i} be made to
mean the same thing as the clunky {gi'e mu'i bo} (which under GIJA would be
{gi je mu'i bo} ? I can see this breaking the case where {broda gi'e mu'i
brode}. However, maybe if we throw in a {bo}, everything becomes okay? e.g.
{.i broda gimu'ibo brode}. I think this works, and doesn't break anything.

Thoughts?

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

